"Enttiku was once one of the old gods, cursed as the child taker and the death dealer."
"Enttiku was born when a daughter kept vigil beside her dying father."
"Enttiku was present when humans first buried their dead; she is about letting go."
"Enttiku offered the rebel mortals her help to become the new pantheon; they left Efestar out."
"In the old war Enttiku kept out of the fight, though Gorok begged her for help."
"Enttiku refused to force Khaton or Maranor, and calls that her most dire error."
"Enttiku had never incarnated, for no vessel was strong enough to hold death."
"At Mornyr Viviane became Enttiku's first avatar, the First of the Death Walkers."
"Enttiku's realm is a mud hut with herbs drying, masks, a fur chair and weak floral tea."
"Enttiku appears as a short plain woman with a square jaw, a scarred brow and graying hair."
"Enttiku keeps the souls of dead children in her hut to play until they are ready to go on."
"Enttiku guides souls to the mysteries beyond and will not answer questions about them."
"In the in-between Enttiku shows as a planet-sized cowled figure, or darkness ringed in gold."
"Enttiku says she saves all she can who deserve it."
"Enttiku saved Viviane's soul from Octas during her elemental ritual."
"Enttiku forbade Viviane to cast her change-based killing spell without Enttiku's consent."
"Enttiku taught Viviane the secret of rotating portals, as an apology."
"Enttiku kept her forbidden repertoire from Viviane until the last war."
